From d78848ade2d5d6514bd7ebd6dba876947051bdd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:14:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] Vizzbox 1.0: the name, identity FM-1_850, its
 installer; CC 104..109 when SEQ MIDI OUT or USB comes back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The name where Vizz had it: the splash (Vizzbox / v1.0 / on Skiff 2.0.1 / Hügelton + community), ABOUT
(VIZZBOX, based on Vizz 2.0 / Skiff 2.0.1 / Felucca), the credits beginning with VIZZBOX (all of Skiff's and
Vizz's kept), the crash screen, the update loader (THE VIZZBOX INSTALLER: its 5 x 7 letters gain X), THEME's
default. USB names and descriptors as they were. A release X.Y is FM-1_8(X+4)Y, Vizzbox 1.0 FM-1_850 (Vizz's
family 8XY, where the installers take X >= 2 for Skiff 2.0 inside), its package vizzbox-X.Y.fwsc; a
development build FM-1_800 as Vizz's.

web/make_vizzbox_installer.py: the one-file installer as Vizz 2.0's, the Vizzbox's words; Skiff's page backs
up only when what it installs is 2.0 or later by its version, and the Vizzbox's 1.0 is Skiff 2.0 inside, so
always. web/test_vizzbox_installer.mjs in Chromium: over Vizz 1.0, a Vizz 1.x, Skiff 1.4 and a development
build the backup, the install, the conversion; over Vizz 2.0, Skiff 2.0.1 and a Vizzbox installed only; Vizz
2.0's installer over a Vizzbox the same; Skiff's own page over a Vizzbox (by its version v1.0) runs the
converter, which writes nothing back to a 2.0 store.

tests/producer_test.c: all six CC 104..109 at once when SEQ MIDI OUT turns on while playing and when USB comes
up again; into the GROOVEBOX CC 104 0 once. The tests that name the firmware follow the name; tests/ui_golden.txt
changes only on splash, ABOUT (and its REC, credits and end) and, in the SKIFF palette, MENU's THEME row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawnvCsrvDZVbc37ZFUY
